{"slug":"india-economic-calendar","path":"india-economic-calendar","kind":"table","page_url":"https://indiamacroindicators.co.in/india-economic-calendar","frequency":null,"title":"India Economic Calendar","description":"Scheduled releases of key Indian economic data and RBI events, with previous and actual values.","headline":{},"source":null,"source_url":null,"date_modified":null,"columns":[{"label":"Date"},{"label":"Day"},{"label":"Time (IST)"},{"label":"Indicator"},{"label":"Category"},{"label":"Frequency"},{"label":"Impact"},{"label":"Previous"},{"label":"Previous period"},{"label":"Actual"},{"label":"Actual period"},{"label":"Expected"},{"label":"Insight"},{"label":"Indicator slug","hidden":true}],"rows":[["2026-10-01","Thursday","10:30","HSBC Manufacturing PMI","Economic Growth","Monthly","High","52.8","2026-08-01","55.1","2026-09-01",null,"A jump of 2.3 points in a single month, after four consecutive months of decline, is a strong reversal and suggests that the manufacturing slowdown was shallower than the trend implied. However, one month of recovery after a prolonged slide is a reason for cautious optimism, not a confirmation that the sector has turned a corner. The next reading will matter more than this one.","hsbc-manufacturing-purchasing-managers-index-pmi"],["2026-10-01","Thursday","17:00","GST Collections","Government Finances","Monthly","Medium","Rs 1,998.5 bn","2026-08-01","Rs 2,035.2 bn","2026-09-01",null,null,"goods-and-services-tax-gst-collections"],["2026-10-06","Tuesday","10:30","HSBC Services PMI","Economic Growth","Weekly","High","54.1","2026-08-01","55.2","2026-09-01",null,"Services PMI rising to 55.2 marks the second consecutive month of improvement, suggesting the sharp July drop was a temporary dip rather than the start of a deeper slowdown. With both manufacturing and services now moving up together for the first time in months, the growth picture is looking more balanced than it has at any point since May, which is a meaningful shift in the overall economic direction.\n","hsbc-services-purchasing-managers-index-pmi"],["2026-10-07","Wednesday","10:00","RBI Monetary Policy Committee","Monetary Policy & Interest Rates","","High","5.25%","2026-08-01","5.50%","2026-09-01",null,"The RBI raised rates by 25 basis points, the first hike after a long pause, confirming that persistently rising inflation has forced the central bank's hand despite signs of economic recovery in both PMIs. A rate hike at a time when manufacturing and services are just beginning to recover tells us the RBI has decided that controlling inflation is more urgent than protecting growth, which changes the outlook for borrowing costs and interest-sensitive sectors for the rest of FY27.\n","repo-rate"],["2026-10-09","Friday","17:00","Foreign Exchange Reserves","Trade & Currency","Monthly","High","$$ 740.8 bn","2026-08-01","$$ 747.6 bn","2026-09-01",null,"Reserves rising for the second consecutive month to $747.6B confirms that the sharp drawdown seen earlier this year has genuinely reversed, and foreign capital is flowing back into India with consistency. Two months of consecutive reserve buildup alongside a rate hike signals that the RBI is now operating from a position of strength rather than pressure, which is a fundamentally different and more stable environment than what existed just three months ago.\n","foreign-exchange-reserves"],["2026-10-12","Monday","16:00","Consumer Price Index (CPI) Inflation","Inflation","Monthly","High","4.8%","2026-08-01","5.5%","2026-09-01",null,"A jump of 0.7 percentage points in a single month takes inflation to its highest level this year, and coming right after a rate hike, it tells us the RBI moved just in time. With inflation now at 5.5% and still rising, the October MPC meeting will almost certainly be another hold, and the possibility of a second hike before year end is now very much on the table.","consumer-price-index-cpi-inflation-headline"],["2026-10-14","Wednesday","12:00","Wholesale Price Index (WPI)","Inflation","Monthly","Low","9.9%","2026-08-01","11.4%","2026-09-01",null,null,"wholesale-price-index-wpi-inflation"],["2026-10-14","Wednesday","17:00","Money Supply (M3)","Inflation","Monthly","Low","17.4%","2026-08-01","19.1%","2026-09-01",null,null,"money-supply-m3"],["2026-10-15","Thursday","16:00","Balance of trade","Trade & Currency","Monthly","Medium","-$ 26.9 bn","2026-08-01","-$ 30.2 bn","2026-09-01",null,null,"merchandise-trade-balance"],["2026-10-15","Thursday","16:00","Unemployment Rate","Jobs & Employment","Monthly","Low","5.0%","2026-08-01","5.0%","2026-09-01",null,null,"unemployment-rate"],["2026-10-16","Friday","17:00","Bank Credit Growth","Banking & Credit","Monthly","Medium","19.2%","2026-08-01","20.6%","2026-09-01",null,null,"bank-credit-growth"],["2026-10-20","Tuesday","17:00","8 core Industries","Economic Growth","Monthly","Medium","5.9%","2026-08-01","7.9%","2026-09-01",null,null,"index-of-industrial-production-iip-8-core-industries"],["2026-10-28","Wednesday","16:00","IIP","Economic Growth","Monthly","Medium","7.8%","2026-08-01","6.7%","2026-09-01",null,null,"index-of-industrial-production-iip-overall"],["2026-10-30","Friday","16:00","Balance of trade","Trade & Currency","Monthly","Medium","$$ 16.5 bn","2026-08-01","$$ 19.2 bn","2026-09-01",null,null,"services-trade-net-inflows"],["2026-10-30","Friday","17:00","Sector-wise Bank Credit","Banking & Credit","Monthly","Low","24.4%","2026-08-01","28.3%","2026-09-01",null,null,"bank-credit-services"],["2026-10-30","Friday","17:00","Government Capital Expenditure","Government Finances","Monthly","High","-29.9%","2026-08-01","-3.1%","2026-09-01",null,null,"government-capital-expenditure"],["2026-11-02","Monday","10:30","HSBC Manufacturing PMI","Economic Growth","Monthly","High","55.1","2026-09-01","54.7","2026-10-01",null,null,"hsbc-manufacturing-purchasing-managers-index-pmi"],["2026-11-02","Monday","17:00","GST Collections","Government Finances","Monthly","Medium","Rs 2,035.2 bn","2026